\frac{13}{11} + \frac{1}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
\frac{78 - 11}{22} \\
\frac{26 + 11}{22}
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
\frac{67}{22} \\
\frac{37}{22}
\end{bmatrix}
$$

---

### Step 6: Compute the distance from $ u $ to the span of $ \{v_1, v_2\} $

The distance from a point $ u $ to the span of $ \{v_1, v_2\} $ is given by:

$$
\text{dist}(u, \text{span}\{v_1, v_2\}) = \| u - \text{proj}(u) \|
$$

We already have:

- $ u = (3, 5, 1, -1) $
- $ \text{proj}(u) = \left( \frac{67}{22}, \frac{37}{22} \right) $

